# Environment Variables for KylaqOBD2Scan
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your actual values.

# =============================================================================
# GEMINI API KEY
# =============================================================================
# Required for AI Doctor (Gemini-powered diagnostic assistant).
# Get your key at: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# IMPORTANT: This key is compiled into the APK as a string literal.
#   - Research/dev builds: fine — extractable but acceptable for personal use.
#   - Production: you MUST restrict the key in Google Cloud Console with
#     Android app package name + SHA-1 of your signing certificate, or
#     move the Gemini call to a backend proxy server.
GEMINI_API_KEY=MY_GEMINI_API_KEY

# =============================================================================
# GOOGLE WEB CLIENT ID (OAuth for Google Sign-In / Drive backup)
# =============================================================================
# Required for Google Sign-In via AndroidX Credential Manager.
# Get your Web Client ID from:
#   https://console.cloud.google.com -> APIs & Services -> Credentials -> OAuth 2.0 Client IDs
#   Create a "Web application" type client, then add Android package + SHA-1.
# Configure in: app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml as 'google_web_client_id'
# Until configured, Google Sign-In is DISABLED.
# GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=your-web-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# =============================================================================
# CRASH AUTO-REPORT TOKEN (GitHub auto-push, optional but instant)
# =============================================================================
# Enables automatic crash -> GitHub Issue with label crash-auto (owner 2026-09-23).
# Without it, crashes still saved to files/crash_logs/ + Drive backup + Firebase Crashlytics.
# With it, next app launch after crash auto-creates Issue that Arena agent can fix without chat upload.
#
# How to create:
# 1. GitHub -> Settings -> Developer settings -> Personal access tokens -> Fine-grained tokens -> New
#    - Repository access: Only select repositories -> tritonelabautomation/KylaqOBD2Scan
#    - Permissions:
#      - Issues: Read and Write
#      - Contents: Read and Write (for crashes/inbox/ commit via dispatch)
#      - Actions: Read and Write (for repository_dispatch)
#      - Metadata: Read (auto)
# 2. Copy token (starts with github_pat_...)
# 3. Add here + as GitHub repo secret (see below)
#
# Where it goes:
# - Local build: this .env file (copy to .env) -> BuildConfig.CRASH_REPORT_TOKEN
#   File location: /home/user/KylaqOBD2Scan/.env  (project root, gitignored)
#   Example: CRASH_REPORT_TOKEN=github_pat_11AXXXXX_XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
# - CI / GitHub Actions: repo Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions -> New repository secret
#   Name: CRASH_REPORT_TOKEN, Value: your token
#   Path in GitHub: https://github.com/tritonelabautomation/KylaqOBD2Scan/settings/secrets/actions
#   Then app/build.gradle.kts injects System.getenv("CRASH_REPORT_TOKEN") into BuildConfig.
#
# Empty = no GitHub push, still local + Drive (fully anonymous fallback).
# CRASH_REPORT_TOKEN=github_pat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
